xbrli:xbrl.ind-as:UsefulLivesOrDepreciationRatesInv:
The useful life of the assets considered for depreciation is summarized below:
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Plant and machinery and computer equipment
2 to 6 years
Furniture and fixtures, Equipment, and other &nbsp;&nbsp;assets
4 to 6 years
Leasehold improvements
To be amortized over the lesser of the period of lease and the useful life of the asset The useful lives and residual values are reviewed by the management at each financial year-end and revised, if appropriate. In case of a revision, the unamortised depreciable amount is charged over the revised remaining useful life. &nbsp;

